# rule.require.inventory-for-enumerable-concepts

when a concept's entries are enumerable — dimensions nameable, positions closed — curate an inventory: one file per cell, addressed by coordinates, every cell accounted for. a prose list, grouped section, or partial catalog over it is a defect.

## .why

- an inventory generates cells from the axes before entries are collected, so an empty cell is a visible gap. a list cannot report absence
- lookup is an address, not a grep
- ref-only (one address per entry), so it scales at fixed cost

| when… | then… |
|---|---|
| a doc enumerates members of one concept | are the dimensions closed? |
| a grouped list whose groups are a dimension | the groups are an axis — inventory |
| you add the Nth entry to a list of N-1 | accretion path. is the space generable? |
| you say "the possible values are …" | a closed dimension declared |

## .the test

1. what are the dimensions, and the positions on each? cannot list them → not inventoriable; build a catalog or `example=` set
2. how many cells, how many occupied? the difference is the gap list. write it in the root's index

## .requires

1. declare axes + closed positions in `inventory.of=$concept._.md`
2. one file per cell (`rule.forbid.itemization-without-coordinates`)
3. classify every cell: occupied, forbidden (an invariant), empty (a gap). never omit one
4. root is an index: axes, counts, gaps; no per-entry narrative
5. new position → re-walk, add a slice

## .boundary

| the concept | the artifact |
|---|---|
| closed, an address per entry suffices | inventory (refs only) |
| closed, reader needs each shape | catalog (inventory + preview per entry) |
| dimensions open-ended | catalog of what is known |
| occurrences on a declared axis (`case`) | inventory over that axis |
| occurrences, no axis | `example=$id` files |

"enumerable" does not mean enumerable in advance: an inventory requires entries addressable and gaps checkable.

blocker: enumerable concept as prose or grouped list · root with no axes · silently omitted cell · open positions · occurrence set under a coined name · per-entry narrative in the root · inventory entries that carry previews.

⇒ `howto.curate-an-inventory` · `rule.forbid.itemization-without-coordinates`
